{
  "_comment": [
    "One row per DeepSeek checkpoint this engine supports.  Read by tools/v41/ckpt.py, which every entry point uses:",
    "the launcher (Start DeepSeek.bat, ds41_local.py), the model menu (pick_model.py), setup (setup-ds41-models.bat,",
    "first-start.bat, setup_space.py) and the converters (v41_sidecar.py, extract_engram.py).  A new checkpoint is one",
    "new row; DS41_CHECKPOINT=<id> selects a row, otherwise 'default'.",
    "fingerprint: the first 16 hex digits of sha256 over the lines 'model-NNNNN-of-NNNNN.safetensors <sha256>\\n' of",
    "every weight shard, sorted by name (ckpt.py fingerprint --repo R --revision REV computes it from Hugging Face's",
    "published hashes).  It names the weights, not the repository commit: a later README or template commit keeps it.",
    "derived: the files built from this checkpoint's weights.  Each one made by setup or a converter gets a stamp",
    "beside it (<file>.ckpt.json: checkpoint id + fingerprint); ds41_local.py warns when a derived file in use was",
    "built from another checkpoint than the model it runs with.  'match' / 'meta_match': how a file without a stamp",
    "is recognised (regular expressions on its file name / on the GGUF's general.* strings), tried row by row in order.",
    "A row's patterns name its own files only: never a bare 'DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-' (a dated checkpoint's files start",
    "with it too) - the base's names continue with a letter, a dated checkpoint's with its digits.  A new row's names",
    "must not match an existing row's patterns, whatever its place in 'order' (tools/v41/test_ckpt.py checks a",
    "made-up 1201 row against every row here)."
  ],
